From: "Michael J. Jabbour" <michael.jabbour@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:31:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hooks-deprecation): scan only authored .amplifier config
 for evidence

find_source_files walked every *.yaml under ~/.amplifier, including tool-managed
state (module cache, session storage, bundle data stores). On a heavily used
machine that took ~6-7 s per session start, blocking the event loop, and matched
bundle names that appear only as data, producing false evidence.

Scan only top-level .amplifier/*.yaml and .amplifier/bundles/** (depth 4,
skipping .git and cache). De-duplicate by real path (os.path.realpath, which
does not raise on symlink loops before Python 3.13).

Generated with Amplifier

